      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62def6ea675a5344c09229e6|full_name}: @{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} @{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name} I get the frustration – VRChat yanking the rug out from under the community like this isn't just inconvenient, it's a slap in the face to both users and chatbox devs. No heads-up, no patch notes, nothing. It's like they're trying to ghost a feature that a chunk of the community actually digs.\n\nAnd sure, security's a big deal, but come on, there's got to be a middle ground. A mute chatbox option, maybe or talk with the chatbox devs how we can solve this.\n\nSomething that lets people opt-out if they're not into the chatbox thing without nixing it for everyone else. It's about choice.\n\nThis feels like a rerun of the whole mod debacle, and not in a good way. Chatbox developers pour time and creativity into these tools, and this silent treatment? That's just low. Users and creators deserve some respect and a say in the game they're a part of. It's about time VRChat remembers that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
